  "published_part_finding": "In the delivered DAVIS partition, `cold_drug` really is ligand-disjoint from `train` (0 of its ligand rows appear in train) but its targets are all warm, while `cold_target` is target-disjoint (88% of its target rows unseen in train) with all ligands warm. `val` is not entity-disjoint at all: 100% of its ligands and 100% of its targets also appear in train. So evaluating on these files tests different things, and a number quoted as 'DAVIS cold-drug' depends on which of the shipped blocks was used.",
